      "content": "To prepare the classic garlic butter pasta, follow these steps:\n\n1. Bring a large pot of salted water to a boil. Use about 1-2 tablespoons of salt for every 4 cups of water. Add 8-12 ounces of your preferred pasta shape (such as spaghetti, linguine, or fettuccine) to the boiling water and cook according to the package instructions until al dente.\n2. While the pasta is cooking, melt 2 tablespoons of unsalted butter in a large skillet over medium heat. Add 2-3 cloves of minced garlic and cook for 1-2 minutes, until fragrant and lightly golden.\n3. Reserve 1 cup of pasta water before draining the cooked pasta. Add the drained pasta to the skillet with the garlic butter and toss everything together until the pasta is well coated with the sauce.\n4. If desired, sprinkle 1/4 cup of grated Parmesan cheese over the pasta and toss again to combine. The heat from the pasta will help melt the cheese and create a creamy sauce.\n5. If the sauce seems too thick, add a little of the reserved pasta water to loosen it up.\n\nThis version incorporates the ingredients more explicitly into the instructions, while still maintaining",
